breached-passwords.txt
======================

Passwords known from data breaches, which identity-auth BRX-IA-CRED-001 requires new passwords
to be checked against. Used by io.brix.platform.identity.security.PasswordPolicy.

Contents: the entries of 8 to 64 characters of "100k-most-used-passwords-NCSC.txt", lower-cased
and de-duplicated (46,483 lines; source SHA-256
c2e5696882c603b76bb67a47ee970897e5a76fc4c3f5547abe3d0ca340c576e0, retrieved 2026-10-24).

Origin of the data:

- The UK National Cyber Security Centre published the 100,000 most common passwords of the
  Pwned Passwords data set of Have I Been Pwned (https://haveibeenpwned.com/Passwords), which is
  made available by Troy Hunt under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence.
- The file was taken from SecLists
  (https://github.com/danielmiessler/SecLists/blob/master/Passwords/Common-Credentials/100k-most-used-passwords-NCSC.txt),
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2018 Daniel Miessler.

